              "Brentford break transfer record with £42m signing of Ouattara",
            content:
              '\n<p><a href="https://www.flashscore.co.uk/team/brentford/xYe7DwID/">Brentford</a> have completed the signing of Dango <a href="https://www.flashscore.co.uk/player/ouattara-dango/GvqREHp3/">Ouattara</a> from Bournemouth for a reported £42 million, the highest fee in the club’s history.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The move surpasses the £30m paid for Igor Thiago last year and could pave the way for Yoane Wissa’s departure.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Ouattara, 23, scored 11 goals in 88 appearances for Bournemouth after joining from Lorient in 2023. &#8220;We’re really happy to get Dango in,&#8221; manager Keith Andrews said. &#8220;We liked his Premier League experience, even at his young age, and he just hasn’t found the rhythm yet because of a lack of consistent game time.&#8221;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The Bees are undergoing major changes after finishing 10th last season. Former boss Thomas Frank is now at <a href="https://www.flashscore.co.uk/team/tottenham/UDg08Ohm/">Tottenham</a>, top scorer Bryan Mbeumo has joined Manchester United, and captain <a href="https://www.flashscore.co.uk/player/norgaard-christian/E3lsxLi7/">Christian Norgaard signed</a> for <a href="https://www.flashscore.co.uk/team/arsenal/hA1Zm19f/">Arsenal</a>. <a href="https://www.flashscore.co.uk/player/wissa-yoane/b35gWzB2/">Wissa</a>, who hit 19 league goals last term, is being linked with <a href="https://www.flashscore.co.uk/team/newcastle/p6ahwuwJ/">Newcastle</a>.</p>\n',
